@AGENTS.md

## Claude Code specifics

- Hooks in `.claude/settings.json`: after every Edit/Write under the source or test
  roots, `scripts/agent/post-edit-tests.mjs` runs `vitest related` for that file and
  reports failures back to you. When you stop, `scripts/agent/stop-check.mjs` runs
  `npm run check -- --fast` and blocks once if it fails. Fix the reported failures;
  do not disable the hooks. A hook that cannot read its input says that tests were
  not run; then run `npm run check -- --fast` yourself.
- Skills in `.claude/skills/`: `implement-requirement`, `debug-in-obsidian`,
  `add-feature`, `write-obsidian-test`. Use them for those workflows.
- Safe commands are pre-approved in exact forms; publishing, force pushes,
  `release:operate` and Obsidian downloads (`--allow-download`,
  `OBSIDIAN_ALLOW_DOWNLOAD`) are denied. When Obsidian is not provisioned, ask the
  user to run the first download themselves; ask before any other network-dependent
  step. Commands that write to a chosen path (`--plan-out`, `--output`,
  `--outputFile`) or act on another folder (`--root`) always ask first.
